 "divergence_note": "Google's C++ matcher (robots_test.cc) implements implementation-specific semantics for some user-agent group constructions (e.g. a prefix group 'foo' matching bot 'FooBot' whose only rule is 'Allow: /some/path' yields DENY for other paths in the C++ reference). Both protego (RFC 9309-style) and urllib.robotparser return ALLOW there. Divergent cases are kept for documentation but not asserted."
